      Core load emulator reads CSR_VTYPE (line 148), extracts VSEW/VLMUL via GET_VSEW/GET_VLMUL (lines 156-157), computes vemul = GET_VEMUL(vlmul, view, vsew) and emul = GET_EMUL(vemul) (lines 164-165). Register indexing at line 229 uses vd + seg * emul with LMUL-derived multiplier. Under Zvvmm, the same vtype LMUL bits encode CMUL = LMUL/λ² for accumulator register groups, so the LMUL-derived emul diverges from the actual C-register group multiplier. set_vreg would silently address wrong banks, enabling tile overlap/corruption. The firmware has no mechanism to detect or reject matrix-configured vtype before entering this path.
  [RISK] lib/sbi/sbi_trap_v_ldst.c:240-332  sbi_misaligned_v_st_emulator
      Mirrors the load path identically: reads CSR_VTYPE (line 248), extracts VSEW/VLMUL (lines 256-257), computes vemul/emul (lines 264-265). At line 307, get_vreg uses vd + seg * emul to index source registers. With matrix-configured vtype, the effective C-register group multiplier (CMUL) diverges from the LMUL-derived emul, so extracted vs2/vd register data may come from wrong indices, producing silent store-data corruption. Same semantic gap as the load emulator.
  [RISK] include/sbi/riscv_encoding.h:1423-1424  GET_VSEW / GET_VLMUL
      GET_VSEW extracts (vtype >> 3) & 0x3; GET_VLMUL extracts vtype & 0x7. These are correct bit-extraction macros and faithfully return hardware values. However, they are the sole mechanism used by the load/store emulators to determine register-group layout, and they have no awareness of the matrix-mode bit in vtype. Under Zvvmm, LMUL bits carry different semantics for C accumulators (CMUL = LMUL/λ²), but these macros silently return the raw LMUL field as if it were standard vector LMUL. The macros themselves are not buggy, but they lack a companion check (e.g., IS_MATRIX_MODE(vtype)) that downstream code would need to disambiguate the interpretation.
  [RISK] include/sbi/riscv_encoding.h:1427-1428  GET_VEMUL / GET_EMUL
      GET_VEMUL computes (vlmul + view - vsew) & 7 — the standard vector identity for non-indexed loads. GET_EMUL converts vemul to 1 << (vemul >= 4 ? 0 : vemul). For matrix operations, the C accumulator group multiplier is CMUL = LMUL/λ² where λ = VLEN/SLEN. This code has no awareness of SLEN or the matrix-mode bit in vtype. The emul derived from these macros is used directly for register-index arithmetic (vd + seg * emul) in both load and store emulators, so the computed index silently uses the wrong group multiplier when vtype is matrix-configured.
